module txsd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.states.texas.{ frcp6-texas }

// The Southern District of Texas's own civil periods, counted under FRCP
// 6. The court may, on its own motion or on application, shorten or extend
// these periods (LR 7.8). The notice of electronic filing is service on
// filing users (LR 5.1). No trigger carries a service method: FRCP 6(d)'s
// three added days follow the manner of service, which is not modeled
// here; the motion periods here run from filing, not service.
//
// Rules that state no period this layer can count stay in notes: the
// judge, not a party, holds the initial pretrial conference and enters a
// scheduling order within 140 days after the filing of a complaint or
// notice of removal, except in the kinds of case LR 16.1 lists; counsel
// discuss ADR with their clients and opposing counsel before the initial
// conference and within 60 days after the deadline for close of discovery
// (LR 16.4(B)(1)); settlements are reported immediately (LR 16.3); no more
// than twenty-five interrogatories, counting sub-parts, may be served
// without leave (LR 33.1), a count, not a document limit. The civil Local
// Rules state no page limit for motions or briefs; the judges' individual
// procedures are not vendored.
//
// The earlier S.D. Tex. outline's FRCP flow belongs to lit/frcp and
// lit/frap; its Supreme Court decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Frow v. De La
// Vega, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Matsushita) are FRCP authority,
// and no reporter text is vendored, so they are removed here.
/// An opposed motion is filed (S.D. Tex. LR 7.3).
event OpposedMotionFiled()
/// The response to an opposed motion is filed (S.D. Tex. LR 7.4).
event ResponseFiled()
/// An order referring the case to ADR is entered (S.D. Tex. LR 16.4).
event AdrOrderEntered()
/// An ADR proceeding is completed (S.D. Tex. LR 16.4).
event AdrCompleted()
/// An exhibit is listed and made available (S.D. Tex. LR 44.1).
event ExhibitListed()
/// Trial (S.D. Tex. LR 46).
event TrialDate()
/// Trial is completed (S.D. Tex. LR 79.2).
event TrialCompleted()
/// A final judgment is entered (S.D. Tex. LR 54.2).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// A bill of costs is filed (S.D. Tex. LR 54.2).
event BillOfCostsFiled()
/// The case is disposed of with no appeal (S.D. Tex. LR 79.2).
event DispositionWithoutAppeal()
/// The clerk gives written notice that exhibits returned by the court of
/// appeals are to be removed (S.D. Tex. LR 79.2).
event ReturnedExhibitsNoticed()

/// S.D. Tex. LR 7.3, 7.4: an opposed motion is submitted to the judge 21
/// days from filing without notice from the clerk and without appearance
/// by counsel, and a response must be filed by the submission day; failure
/// to respond is taken as a representation of no opposition.
deadline response-period: 21.days after OpposedMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "S.D. Tex. LR 7.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 7.4(E): unless the presiding judge directs otherwise, the
/// movant may file a reply brief within 7 days from the date the response
/// is filed.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "S.D. Tex. LR 7.4"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 16.4(E): a party opposing the ADR referral, method or
/// appointed provider files written objections, with its reasons, within
/// ten days of entry of the order for ADR.
deadline adr-objection-period: 10.days after AdrOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 16.4"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 16.4(K): within 14 days of completion of the ADR
/// proceeding, the parties jointly file a memorandum stating what the rule
/// lists, including whether the case settled and the provider's fees; it
/// does not apply to non-binding arbitration under 28 U.S.C. § 654.
deadline adr-report-period: 14.days after AdrCompleted() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 16.4"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 44.1: a party requiring authentication of an exhibit
/// notifies the offering party in writing within 7 days after the exhibit
/// is listed and made available; failure to object in writing before trial
/// concedes authenticity.
deadline authentication-objection-period: 7.days after ExhibitListed() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 44.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 46: objections to the admissibility of exhibits are made at
/// least 7 days before trial, in writing, with copies of the disputed
/// exhibit and authority.
deadline admissibility-objection-period: 7.days before TrialDate() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 46"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 54.2: a bill of costs, with any application for attorney's
/// fees taxable as costs, is filed within 14 days of the entry of a final
/// judgment.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 54.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 54.2: objections to the bill, the attorney's fees or both
/// are filed within 7 days of the bill's filing.
deadline bill-of-costs-objection-period: 7.days after BillOfCostsFiled() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 54.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 79.2(A): exhibits not easily stored in a file folder are
/// withdrawn within 7 days after the completion of the trial, and reduced
/// reproductions or photographs substituted.
deadline oversized-exhibit-withdrawal: 7.days after TrialCompleted() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 79.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 79.2(B): if there is no appeal, the offering party removes
/// its exhibits within thirty days after disposition of the case; exhibits
/// not removed are disposed of by the clerk at the offering party's
/// expense.
deadline exhibit-removal: 30.days after DispositionWithoutAppeal() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 79.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// S.D. Tex. LR 79.2(B): when there is an appeal, exhibits returned by the
/// court of appeals are removed by the offering party within 14 days after
/// written notice from the clerk.
deadline returned-exhibit-removal: 14.days after ReturnedExhibitsNoticed() counted_by frcp6-texas cite "S.D. Tex. LR 79.2"
{
  forum frcp
}
